            <ArticleTitle>Spinal shock in spontaneous cervical spinal epidural haematoma.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1161-2; discussion 1162-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A young man presented with quadriparesis and spinal shock because of a spontaneous cervical spinal epidural haematoma was reported. Immediate MRI diagnosis followed by emergency decompression with six hours of presentation resulted in complete recovery.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
